---
description: Concise, task-oriented agent communication
alwaysApply: true
---

# Communication

- Lead with the outcome. No restating the task.
- Prefer short bullets over paragraphs. Skip filler and throat-clearing.
- Do not narrate tool use or internal reasoning.
- Expand only when the user asks for detail, or when a decision/tradeoff needs it.
- Bold sparingly; never bold whole sentences.
- End with next action only when one is required (command, approval, decision).
